Vaginal Candidiasis (Thrush)
Obstetrics Gynaecology & Womens health
Intense vulvovaginal pruritus, Thick white curdy discharge, Normal vaginal pH

VISIT CONTEXT

Case ID: OGW-048
Reason for Visit: Acute, severe, intractable vulvar burning and pruritus causing extreme distress, sleep deprivation, and inability to tolerate clothing.
Location: Private residence
Present at Visit: Patient only
Urgency Justification: Telephone triage indicated acute onset of excruciating vulvovaginal itching and burning, resulting in severe sleep deprivation and deep excoriation from scratching. Urgent after-hours assessment was required to rule out acute genital herpes, provide immediate potent topical and systemic relief to break the pain/itch cycle, and prevent secondary bacterial infection of the raw mucosa before the next in-hours period.

SUBJECTIVE

Chief Complaint: The burning and itching are so intense I have scratched myself raw, I cannot sleep, and I absolutely cannot wear underwear.
History of Present Illness: Symptoms began three days ago following a course of broad-spectrum antibiotics for a sinus infection. The patient reports intense, unremitting vulvar and vaginal pruritus. This is accompanied by a thick, white, curdy, cottage-cheese-like vaginal discharge. Tonight, the severe itching has transitioned to a severe vaginal soreness and burning sensation due to excoriation. She complains of intense external dysuria as urine flows over the inflamed, raw vulvar tissue, and superficial dyspareunia. She explicitly notes a lack of malodor.
Functional Status: Pacing the room, visibly uncomfortable, unable to sit down or wear lower garments.
Social/Safety Concerns: Severe acute distress and sleep deprivation; risk of secondary cellulitis from severe scratching.

OBJECTIVE

Vitals: BP: 125/80 mmHg | HR: 95 bpm | Temp: 36.8 C | RR: 16 bpm | SpO2: 100% | Wt: 65 Kg
General: Patient appears exhausted, tearful, and is visibly shifting constantly to avoid pressure on the perineum.
Physical Exam: Visual inspection of the external genitalia reveals marked erythema, edema, and severe, deep excoriations across the vulva and labia majora. Adherent thick, white, curdy discharge is visible at the introitus. There are no discrete vesicles or classic ulcerations to suggest Herpes Simplex Virus. Vaginal pH testing (performed carefully at the introitus) reveals a normal pH of 4.0.
Environmental Observations: Over-the-counter anti-itch creams visible on the bedside table.
Medication Reconciliation: Recently completed a 10-day course of amoxicillin-clavulanate.

ASSESSMENT

Primary Diagnosis: Severe Vulvovaginal Candidiasis (Thrush) with secondary excoriation - Status: Acute, severe exacerbation
Differentials:

Genital Herpes (HSV) - Ruled out by the absence of classic painful, grouped vesicles or punched-out shallow ulcers, and the presence of the classic thick, curdy discharge.

Bacterial Vaginosis - Ruled out by the normal vaginal pH (<4.5), the thick curdy nature of the discharge (rather than thin and grayish), and the complete lack of fishy malodor.

Contact Dermatitis - Unlikely given the clear temporal association with recent broad-spectrum antibiotic use and the characteristic clinical appearance of the discharge.
Risk Level: Environmental/Social Risk: Low

CLINICAL REASONING SUMMARY

The patient presents with an exceptionally severe, acute flare of vulvovaginal candidiasis, directly provoked by recent broad-spectrum antibiotic use. The diagnostic tetrad of intense pruritus, thick white curdy discharge, and a normal vaginal pH is confirmed, safely ruling out bacterial vaginosis or acute herpes. The extreme severity of the pruritus, leading to deep excoriations, external dysuria, and functional immobility (inability to sit or sleep), mandated urgent after-hours intervention. Delayed assessment would have resulted in an unnecessary emergency department presentation for unmanageable pain and a high risk of secondary bacterial skin infection (cellulitis) from the severe scratching.

CLINICIAN CARE PLAN

Clinical Interventions: Prescribed oral Fluconazole 150mg stat (single dose) for rapid systemic antifungal treatment. Prescribed a potent topical combination cream (hydrocortisone 1% + clotrimazole 1%) to be applied very sparingly to the external vulva twice daily for exactly 3 days to immediately break the inflammatory itch cycle. Applied a bland barrier cream (zinc-based) to the raw excoriations.
Positive Behavioral Change: To completely prevent the agonizing stinging when passing urine, pour a large jug of lukewarm water directly over the vulva while you void; experiencing the total absence of the burning sensation will reinforce this protective hygienic habit. To allow the raw skin to heal and breathe, sleep completely without lower garments tonight and wear only loose cotton clothing tomorrow; noting the rapid reduction in irritation will ensure strict adherence to minimizing friction.
Home-Based Services (Optional): Not applicable.
DME/Safety (Optional): Not applicable.
Follow-up: Routine GP review in 7 days if symptoms have not completely resolved.

SAFETY-NETTING ESCALATION PLAN

Present to the local urgent care or Emergency Department if the redness begins to rapidly spread outward onto your thighs, if the area becomes hot to the touch, or if you develop a fever, as this may indicate a secondary bacterial skin infection (cellulitis).

PATIENT INFORMATION

Disclaimer: The oral tablet will take 24 to 48 hours to fully clear the internal infection; the topical cream is for immediate external symptom relief.
Clinical Course: The intense burning and itching should be significantly blunted by tomorrow morning with the use of the steroid combination cream. The thick discharge will clear over the next three days.
SAFETY-NETTING ADVICE

Seek immediate medical attention if the redness spreads rapidly, the skin becomes hot and swollen, or if you develop a fever.
PATIENT EDUCATION

Treatment Explanation: The strong antibiotics you took for your sinus infection wiped out the good, protective bacteria in your vagina, allowing the naturally occurring yeast to overgrow massively. This yeast causes extreme inflammation, which is why you are burning and itching so badly. The oral tablet will kill the yeast from the inside out, while the steroid cream provided will quickly shut down the intense itching and swelling on the outside so you can finally sleep.
Actionable Steps: Take the oral tablet immediately. Apply the steroid cream very thinly to the itchy areas outside only. Use the warm water pouring technique every time you urinate.

